        <ArticleTitle>[Use of fibrin glue in gynecologic operations].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Anastomosing of the uterine horns in 98 experimental rats has employed a fibrin glue FK-1 (USSR) and Beriplast (FRG) or microsurgical techniques in a control group. Intactness and sealing of the anastomoses and the incidence of pelvic adhesions were assessed at 5 minutes, 1 hour and 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 days following the operation. The fibrin glue Beriplast was used clinically in 6 patients during reconstructive-plastic operations. The results with seamless anastomosing of uterine horns in rats using the fibrin glue and preliminary clinical evidence suggests a high effectiveness of the glue in gynecologic reconstructive plastic surgery.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
